==Strategy==
If you thought this Otherworld Colosseum would just be a complete pushover, don't worry. This stage contains a brutal gauntlet of Traitless enemies that makes 3 Crown [[Cloned Farmers]] look like a joke.

As with the other stages in this Otherworld Colosseum, your pick of [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] helps ensure ample cash flow, and thus cash is not a pressing concern here, and you can even do without them. However, the boss, Kappy Jr. is paired with a nightmarish supporting cast. The Wild Doges and Sir Rels help push alongside Kappy Jr, while Bore Jr can blast your entire army to smithereens if unanswered, and Dolphina, Mega BaaBaa and Camelle put even more pressure. The most annoying support in this stage, however, is Henry, as he has a devastating Freeze proc, turning your cats into sitting ducks.

While rolling with an Anti-Surge loadout is definitely a consideration, you could also try to brute force through the enemy composition. Either way, [[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]] is almost mandatory here, due to his strong anti-Traitless stats and the fact that he benefits from the colosseum ruleset.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Both of these units have [[Double Bounty]], allowing them to help generate more income.
*[[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]]: Cop Cat benefitting from the colosseum ruleset, paired with his anti-Traitless stats makes him pretty much mandatory here if you don't have strong Uber Rares to carry you.
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Ironcat]]: Ironcat is a useful support unit here, being able to Weaken Kappy Jr., block Bore Jr.'s wave attacks and momentarily stall the enemy frontline. Keep him away from the Sir Rels, however.
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]: Slapstick Cats are very useful here, as they benefit from the ruleset and can take care of the Sir Rels, while having good general stats to put in work against the Traitless enemies here.
*[[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]]: If owned, Brainwashed Flying Cat makes this stage a cakewalk. It benefits from the ruleset, has a very fast cooldown, has extreme anti-Traitless damage, a guaranteed Slow and an immunity to Waves and Surges.
*[[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Eraser Cat:]] Very tanky meatshield against traitless, also a super rare too making it much more effective. Just make sure he doesn't get cursed too much.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Awakened Bahamut Cat can help create bursts of damage for a lot of value. He pairs very well with Ironcat here, as Ironcat can Weaken Kappy Jr. while nullifying Bore Jr., helping Bahamut get more hits.
*Research [[Cat Combo]]s: Cat Combos with a Research effect, such as [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] are very helpful here, helping spawn your units, especially Cop Cat, more frequently.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Death's Daughter Lunacia]]: Death's Daughter Lunacia is a very potent option for this stage, packing an immunity to Freeze, Strong Against Traitless and Weaken. With [[Surge Attack#Counter-Surge|Counter-Surge]], she can use Kappy Jr.'s Surge Attacks to her advantage and rampage through the enemy composition.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: With Surge and Freeze immunity and a piercing Omni-strike, Oni Battlepod will absolutely destroy [[Dolphina]], [[Kappy Jr.]] and all the other traitless threats here, and  can abuse [[Camelle]]'s fast attack rate to rebound constantly and destroy everything.

